rf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 31% of normal on the middle, while April to May hit 191%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 39% on the middle. Grid 19341 had its driest year in 1963 at 51%.</p>"}
